Why does everybody seem to want to make Hack impossible for new players?!

I am very new to Hack, and often dont know what you mean by getting to
hell, or the wizard etc..

 But I know this much! I find it a little too hard at the start, but far
too easy at the end, and this part of the game should be made more
difficult. But *NOT* in the sense that most of you are suggesting. No way
should you get rid of polypiling. Or give WoP's only 1 charge. Dont
forget there are other people that arent such *experts* as some of you,
and making it harder for you, will make it feel impossible to new
players.

I believe there should be seperate sort of "missions" in the
game, whether it is being transported at level xx to another totally
different dungeon in which you have to please your god or something like
that. Like the castle, and Medusa, and those seperate sections of the
game.
Perhaps introduce more new characters, or increase the power of
current ones. I have gotten to the castle, in which downstairs of ceased
to exist. I would never ever have figured out how to go down a level from
there, had I not read it on here. Perhaps some (more?) hints written on the
floor in places like this?
 Like - " Teleportation is the way... ".
 Or new scrolls, that arent magic, but information..

 The game should be made so the individual player, can restrict *himself*
not the game restricting him. Otherwise it is beyond new players, and
NetHack will "die"..

 For all those people who have suggested getting rid of polymorph, or
some other part of the game, in an effort to make it harder for them, why
dont you restrict yourself. Like not using poly-piling..

Now here is a thought for the dev team :
What about after the question on what race/profession you would like to be at
the start, have another question/option, on what level you would like to
be..so if you find it to easy, then increase this "difficulty" level..


